Subject: [PATCH] Zygote: seccomp filters of the apps installed while SELinux is permissive

Zygote skipped the seccomp filters (app, app zygote, system, setuid/setgid range) when SELinux was
not enforcing ("seccomp disabled by setenforce 0"). SELinux stays permissive on the Pocket DS, so
no app had a seccomp filter: a security layer less, and root checkers report "Seccomp: disabled".
gIsSecurityEnforced only decides that, it is now always true: the filters are installed as on
any device. KernelSU lifts them itself for the processes it grants root.

--- a/core/jni/com_android_internal_os_Zygote.cpp
+++ b/core/jni/com_android_internal_os_Zygote.cpp
@@ -2895,7 +2895,9 @@
 
   // security_getenforce is not allowed on app process. Initialize and cache
   // the value before zygote forks.
-  gIsSecurityEnforced = security_getenforce();
+  // PocketDS: SELinux stays permissive on this console, and the value only decides whether the
+  // seccomp filters of the apps are installed: they are installed in any case, as on any device.
+  gIsSecurityEnforced = true;
 
   selinux_android_seapp_context_init();
 
